The '''Gomu Gomu no Mi'''{{Qref|name=named}} is a [[Paramecia]]-type [[Devil Fruit]]{{Qref|name=type revealed}} that grants the user's body the properties of rubber, effectively making them a {{Nihongo|'''Rubber Human'''|ゴム人間|Gomu Ningen|English: "Rubber Man/Person"}}.{{Qref|name=named}}

Originally, the fruit was called the '''Hito Hito no Mi, Model: Nika''' and classified as a [[Zoan#Mythical Zoan|Mythical Zoan]]-type fruit that allows one to transform into the legendary "Sun God" [[Nika]] (and gain his rubbery attributes), before being renamed and reclassified by the [[World Government]] to hide the truth.{{Qref|name=true nature|chap=1044|page=4-5|ep=1071}} In the present, only a few are aware of the fruit's true nature, and its existence was never known to be recorded anywhere.{{Qref|chap=1069|page=8-9|ep=1100|Vegapunk explains the mystery around the fruit's existence and admits he does not know anything about its existence.}}

[[Void Century|Around 900 years ago]], the fruit was eaten by a mysterious figure known as [[Joy Boy]], the first ever [[pirate]] in [[World Timeline|history]].{{Qref|name=c1114}} 13 years ago, the World Government had managed to capture and secure the fruit after chasing it for over 800 years. However, during transport, it was stolen by [[Shanks]] and his [[Red Hair Pirates|crew]].{{Qref|name=c1017|chap=1017|page=17|ep=1039|Who's-Who reveals his past.}}{{Qref|name=c1018|chap=1018|page=7|ep=1040|Who's-Who confirms that the Gomu Gomu no Mi was stolen by the Red Hair Pirates.}}{{Qref|name=named}} Shortly after, it was heedlessly eaten by the series' protagonist, [[Monkey D. Luffy]].{{Qref|name=eaten}} 

==Etymology==
*{{Nihongo|''Gomu''|ゴム}} means "rubber" in Japanese, being borrowed from the Dutch word ''gom'' ("gum").
*{{Nihongo|''Hito''|人}} is Japanese for "person/human (being)".
*{{Nihongo|''Nika''|ニカ}}, a nonstandard Japanese onomatopoeia for "smiling" or "grinning", represents the smiling legendary figure known as "Sun God" Nika, which the fruit is originally named after.
*In the [[VIZ Media|VIZ]] manga, [[4Kids Entertainment|4Kids]] and [[Funimation]] adaptations, it is called the '''Gum-Gum Fruit''', "gum" being a soft, cohesive substance designed for chewing, with elastic properties, and its original name is called the '''Human-Human Fruit, Model: Nika'''.

==Appearance==
The Gomu Gomu no Mi is a violet, spherical shaped fruit, similar to a cantaloupe, with a stem sprouting out of the top, with swirls that go in a curly "S" like-pattern. Its overall appearance greatly resembles a {{W|Yubari King}}.{{Qref|name=named}}

While its final design has the characteristic Devil Fruit swirls all over it, the fruit was initially drawn without them in the first version of Romance Dawn.{{Qref|oneshot=RD1|the Gomu Gomu no Mi is shown without any swirls in the first version of Romance Dawn.}}

In promotional material for the [[One Piece - Defeat Him! The Pirate Ganzack#Release and Reception|1998 Jump Super Anime Tour]], which included the [[One Piece - Defeat Him! The Pirate Ganzack|first animated ''One Piece'' project]], the Gomu Gomu no Mi is depicted green, as the now-well-known violet design had yet to be established.{{Qref|''One Piece - Defeat Him! The Pirate Ganzack'' x ''Hunter x Hunter Pilot'' x ''Seikimatsu Leader Gaiden Takeshi!'' promotional pamphlet}} This design was later reused in the [[Episode 542|''Toriko x One Piece Collab Special 2'']],{{Qref|ep=542|''Toriko x One Piece Collab Special 2''}} potentially as a reference to the original use.

