The '''Supa Supa no Mi''' is a [[Paramecia]]-type [[Devil Fruit]] that enables the user's body to gain characteristics of a steel blade to attack opponents with, making the user a {{Nihongo|'''Full-Body Bladed Human'''|全身刃物人間|Zenshin Hamono Ningen|VIZ: "Human Sword"}}.{{Qref|name=c190p7|chap=190|page=7|ep=116|Daz explains his Devil Fruit ability.}} It was eaten by former [[Baroque Works]] agent and current [[Cross Guild]] member [[Daz Bonez]], also known by his alias Mr. 1.

The fruit's powers were first seen being used by Daz to slice a wall he was about to hit, after he had been kicked by [[Bentham|Mr. 2]].{{Qref|name=c160}} The fruit's powers were fully revealed during his battle with [[Roronoa Zoro]].{{Qref|name=c190p7}}

This fruit's abilities were duplicated in the [[Seraphim|Seraph]] [[S-Hawk]], via a transfusion of [[Green Blood]].{{Qref|name=c1076|chap=1076|page=4|ep=1108|S-Hawk turns his leg into a blade.}}

==Etymology==
*{{Nihongo|''Supasupa''|すぱすぱ/スパスパ}} is a Japanese onomatopoeia for repetitive, clean slicing motions.
*{{Nihongo|''Supari''|すぱり/スパリ}} is onomatopoeic for a single, clean cut.
*In English translations, it is called the '''Dice-Dice Fruit'''.

==Appearance==
The Supa Supa no Mi resembles a bunch of bananas. Each banana resembles a [[sword]] blade with a wavy {{W|Hamon (swordsmithing)|''hamon''}}: The white portion is the sharp edge of a sword, while the dark gray section represents the blunt side. The latter sections contain the various swirls typical of Devil Fruits.{{Qref|magazine=18}}

==Strengths and Weaknesses==
[[File:Supa Supa no Mi Usage.png|thumb|210px|left|Daz demonstrating the ability of the fruit.]]

The major strength of the fruit, as demonstrated by Daz, is that its user can create strong blades from any part of their body.{{Qref|chap=190|page=6-7, 9|ep=116|Daz creates blades on his forearms, elbows, and fingers.}}{{Qref|chap=194|page=12|ep=119|Zoro realizes that Daz can turn any part of his body into a blade.}} The ability allows the user's body to gain characteristics of steel, more specifically a blade. The user is immune to most slashing attacks and can cut through almost anything, from flesh to stone.{{Qref|chap=193|page=17-18|ep=118|Daz demonstrates an immunity to normal sword attacks due to his steel body.}}{{Qref|name=no swordsman|chap=194|page=2|ep=119|Daz claims that no swordsman has been able to cut him since he ate the Supa Supa no Mi.}} 

The user seems to have the ability to cut through objects without the need to physically touch them, much like flying slashes used by various [[Swordsman|swordsmen]]. This has been shown through Daz's Atomic Spurt, Spar Break and Spar Claw, the latter in at least one instance.{{Qref|name=c190|chap=190|page=4-5|ep=116|Daz splits a pillar into vertical segments without touching it while attacking Nami with Spar Claw.}} Also, as demonstrated by moves like Daz's Spiral Hollow, the user can also make the blades spin like saws or drills.{{Qref|name=spiral hollow|chap=195|page=7-10|ep=119|Daz uses Spiral Hollow against Zoro.}}

[[File:Mihawk Defeats Daz.png|thumb|210px|Mihawk cutting through Daz's defense.]]

However, the user's ability to resist slicing attacks is limited as Daz is unable to easily manipulate the hardness of the steel blades. So, while the user is generally immune to most blade attacks, any sword strike strong enough to cut steel is sufficient to slice the user's flesh.{{Qref|chap=195|page=20-21|ep=119|Zoro cuts down Daz.}} Aside from this, the standard Devil Fruit weaknesses apply.{{Qref|chap=557|page=7|ep=466|Daz falls into the water along with other Devil Fruit users.}}

==Usage==
===Daz Bonez===
[[File:Daz Vs. Marines.png|thumb|left|210px|Daz incorparating martial arts with his blades.]]

As an [[assassin]] and [[Martial Artist|martial artist]], Daz primarily uses the fruit's bestowed powers for combat, using them both for defense and offense. His style consists mainly of slashes, chops and acrobatic kicks that are further enhanced by the effects of his Devil Fruit. He also has the ability to sprout blades on the soles of his feet, allowing him to skate on solid ground as if it were ice.

In spite of his heavy reliance in blades, Daz does not consider himself a [[swordsman]]. Also, until he met [[Roronoa Zoro]], Daz had claimed that no swordsman had ever so much as put a scratch on his body.{{Qref|name=no swordsman}} For this reason, Daz intentionally let his guard down and goaded Zoro into attempting to cut him down multiple times during that fight, confident that the pirate hunter would be unable to wound him, which allowed for his eventual defeat. 

====Techniques====
The techniques used by Daz all contain {{Nihongo|'''"Supa"'''|スパ}} in their Japanese name. In the Viz Manga and 4Kids dub, this play on words is absent.

[[Image:Spider.png|thumb|210px|Spider.]]

*{{Nihongo|'''Spider'''|{{Ruby|斬人|スパイダー}}|Supaidā|literally meaning "Slash-/Cutting Man"}}: Remaining completely motionless, Daz hardens his body and becomes impervious to harm, similar in principle to [[Tekkai]]. This was first seen during Daz and Zoro's battle.{{Qref|chap=193|page=17|ep=118|Daz uses Spider to defend himself from Zoro's attack.}} This is called '''Iron Guard''' in the VIZ Manga and 4Kids dub and '''Spider Defense''' in the Funimation dub. In the Funimation subs, it keeps its name.{{-}}

[[File:Spar Claw.png|thumb|210px|Spar Claw.]]

*{{Nihongo|'''Spar Claw'''|{{Ruby|掌握斬|スパークロー}}|Supā Kurō|literally meaning "Grasping Slash/Cut"}}: Daz turns the undersides of his fingers into blades before slashing at his opponent. If he performs this move with enough force, he can even split objects behind his intended target. While the attack's name is mentioned in the manga, it is unnamed in the anime. This was first seen when Daz was attacking Nami,{{Qref|name=c190}} but was named during his battle with Zoro.{{Qref|chap=194|page=4-5|ep=119|Daz uses Spar Claw against Zoro.}} In the VIZ Manga, this is called '''Razor Claws'''. In the Funimation adaptations, it keeps its name.{{-}}

[[File:Sparkling Daisy.png|thumb|210px|Sparkling Daisy.]]

*{{Nihongo|'''Sparkling Daisy'''|{{Ruby|発泡雛菊斬|スパークリングデイジー}}|Supākuringu Deijī|literally meaning "Foaming Daisy Slash/Cut"}}: After turning the insides of his hands and fingers into blades, Daz places his hands together wrist-to-wrist before lunging at his opponent, whom he simultaneously stabs and slices with his hands. The sheer force behind this attack causes Daz to not only cut his intended target but things behind his target as well. This was first seen during Daz and Zoro's battle.{{Qref|chap=194|page=13-14|ep=119|Daz uses Sparkling Daisy against Zoro.}} In the VIZ Manga and 4Kids dub, this is called '''Daisy Blade'''. In the Funimation adaptations, it keeps its name.

