The '''Yomi Yomi no Mi''' is a [[Paramecia]]-type [[Devil Fruit]] which strengthens the user's soul to the point where they resurrect after their first death, allowing them to live a second time and to use several other [[soul]]-based abilities, making the user a {{Nihongo|'''Reviving Human'''|復活人間|Fukkatsu Ningen|Funimation: "Revive Man"}}.{{Qref|name=revived}} It was eaten by [[Brook]].

==Etymology==
*The fruit's name comes from {{Nihongo|'''''yomi'''gaeru''|蘇る・甦る}}, meaning "to be reborn, reanimated, resurrected, resuscitated" in Japanese.
**Said term is derived from {{Nihongo|''yomi''|黄泉}}, which refers to the {{W|Yomi|Japanese underworld}}, and {{Nihongo|''kaeru''|帰る}}, meaning "to return" (with ''kaeru'' changing to ''gaeru'' as an instance of rendaku), thus reflecting this fruit's power to return from the afterlife.
*In the [[VIZ Media|VIZ]] manga and [[Funimation]] adaptations, it is called the '''Revive-Revive Fruit'''.

==Appearance==
The Yomi Yomi no Mi is a spherical-shaped golden fruit with a green stem. On its bottom, it has four stubby growths, making the shape resemble a skull. As with most Devil Fruits, it has swirl patterns allover.{{Qref|magazine=8|page=83|The Yomi Yomi no Mi is shown.}}

==Strengths and Weaknesses==
[[File:Brook's Soul Finding His Body.png|thumb|220px|left|Brook's soul finds and enters his body despite it having already decomposed.]]

The major strength of the fruit, as demonstrated by Brook, is that it gives its user another chance at life after dying once before and thereby a literal second chance at living. After death, the user continues to exist in whatever state they were revived as and can even go as far as to grant a form of "immortality" that lasts until the user suffers a second death. However, since the main attribute of the fruit is resurrection, the Yomi Yomi no Mi's power will remain dormant until the time when the consumer suffers his or her first death. As a result, until such time, the only aspects the fruit bestows upon its eater are the typical Devil Fruit weaknesses.{{Qref|name=revived}}

While the Fruit allows the user's soul to return from the {{Nihongo|"land of the dead"|黄泉の国|yomi no kuni}}, it does not automatically return them to the physical body that it once resided in during its mortal life. Thus, it is then up to the disembodied soul to search for the corporeal body in order to once again reunite with it. Though the user gains another life, their body, however, will continue being a lifeless corpse and will continue rotting away until the user's soul can find its way back to the body. When the user's soul returns to their body, the powers of the Devil Fruit will fortunately support the user's well-being in the case that their body may be in a condition unable to support life.{{Qref|name=revived}}

While the fruit can make the user an undead being of sorts, it, however, grants the user the ability to still feel pain as proof that they have been truly resurrected back to life, regardless of what physical condition they have been revived in.{{Qref|name=c487|chap=487|ep=380|Brook feels pain for the first time in his skeletal state and remembers Yorki's words that pain is proof of "life".}} This is noteworthy because it separates the power of the Yomi Yomi no Mi from the [[zombie]]s created by the [[Kage Kage no Mi]] because although both powers work to make the dead come "alive" again, the Kage Kage no Mi zombies do not feel pain because they are not truly "alive" at all. Brook's susceptibility to sensation seems to be selective, since Brook was able to traverse Punk Hazard's frozen terrain without any signs of discomfort, while the rest of the Straw Hats were shivering in comparison.{{Qref|chap=662|page=10|ep=587}} Earlier during their travel to Fish-Man Island, he did chill at the ocean level.

It may possibly be that Brook is immune to damage that is based on impacting one's tissue, as he carried a petrified [[Kin'emon]] out of the new [[H2S]] compound without much incident. It has been shown that sleeping gas does affect him.{{Qref|chap=656|page=16|ep=580}}{{Qref|chap=669|page=4-5|ep=595}} Another case of this comes from Brook showcasing immunity towards electrocution on at least two different occasions.{{Qref|chap=890|ep=864|Brook survives a lightning bolt from [[Zeus]] to protect Nami, claiming his lack of flesh makes him immune.}}{{Qref|name=c476|chap=476|ep=370|Brook survives being electrocuted in a combo against Oars.}} 

[[File:Brook Releases His Soul From His Body.png|thumb|210px|Brook manifesting his soul from his body.]]

Brook demonstrated a new power of his Devil Fruit on Fish-Man Island after the timeskip. Brook's soul that came back to inhabit his skeleton is still able to leave the body, usually by exiting his mouth, similar to {{W|Astral projection|astral projection}}, and move it everywhere he wants to. It can even pass through walls, similar to [[Perona]]'s own [[Horo Horo no Mi|astral projection power]]. In the anime it was shown as Brook repeating the word "bone" multiple times like a mantra of some sort, and then his spectral form leaves through his mouth, leaving his body seemingly colorless.

When Brook is in spectral form, it mostly resembles his skeletal face (complete with the omega letter-shaped crack across his forehead) and is engulfed in spiritual flames; it appears to be not only visible but also audible to both people and animals since [[Roronoa Zoro|Zoro]] and [[Usopp]] were seen being able to converse with Brook while in this form, and [[Pappag]] was shown scampering away from Brook in this state, mistaking the skeleton's soul as a ghost, therefore frightening the starfish. It is currently unknown as to how far Brook can maintain this separation of his soul from his body or if there are any limits about it at all (i.e., when Perona uses her own spectral form, she leaves her corporeal body dormant).{{Qref|name=c629|chap=629|ep=549|Brook demonstrates his new-found ability to detach his soul from his body.}} However, the main weakness to this ability is that while Brook has his soul out of his body, he cannot use or move his physical body and has to have someone guard him so that Brook won't be harmed.

[[File:Yomi Yomi No Saiken.gif|thumb|210px|left|Brook's soul reattaching his head after decapitation.]]

During his fight with [[Zeo]], Brook reveals that in the past two years he has come to know the true power of his Devil Fruit.{{Qref|name=c643|chap=643|page=7-9|ep=565|Brook explains the true extent of the fruit's ability.}} The soul of a human that died is supposed to go to the land of the dead and stay there, but for his soul to exist in the human world, it emits a powerful energy. Therefore, the power that allows him to live in the human world is neither organs nor muscles, but rather his [[soul]]; the fruit's influence enhances such to make the impossible possible. As long as his bones are not hurt, any attacks will not go to his core. When Zeo beheaded Brook, his soul managed to repair it and connect his bones together again. He has also displayed that he can transfer this energy to an object like his cane sword, in which he summons the {{Nihongo|'''Chill of the Underworld'''|黄泉の冷気|Yomi no Reiki}}, allowing him to freeze his opponent with ice created from his soul's energy. Lastly, he has stated that he can feel the souls of others and, when mixed with his music, is able to move them.{{Qref|chap=635|page=5-6|ep=556}}

[[File:Brook Defeats the Chess Soldiers.png|thumb|210px|Brook using his own soul to counter the effects of the Soru Soru no Mi.]]

This fruit also gives the user certain advantages over the user of the [[Soru Soru no Mi]]; Brook is capable of using the raw energy and presence of his own powerful soul to overwhelm the [[homies]] due to them being created from small pieces of souls that do not belong to them. The effects of this are visually similar to [[Haki/Supreme King Haki|Supreme King Haki]]; it renders the homies unconscious and immobile.{{Qref|chap=848|page=14-15|ep=814|Brook overwhelms the Homies with his soul.}} This advantage is decreased against homies made from Big Mom's own soul, as Brook cannot overwhelm them, but he is capable of injuring them as well to varying degrees.{{Qref|chap=853|page=2-3|ep=820|Big Mom states that Brook cannot defeat Homies that have her own soul within them.}}{{Qref|chap=890|page=16-17|ep=864|Brook cuts the cloud homie Zeus in half.}}

==Usage==
While the fruit's only major bestowed power is only usable after death, its secondary powers however are rather useful in keeping Brook basically "alive". Through the fruit's powers, Brook is able to function without the presence of necessary and vital body parts that have decomposed long ago. He is able to interact with the environment around him without the presence of eyeballs or any other sensory organ to aid him. Brook, in particular, retains his ability of speech despite his vocal cords and even his windpipe having long since rotted away. He is able to taste and digest food like any other normal living thing to sustain himself. Drinking milk in particular rapidly heals him as the calcium intake repairs any of Brook's bones that may have been broken in battle (an effect non-canonically referred to as {{Nihongo|'''Kanso-Kyoku Preparation'''{{Qref|game=PW4}}|間奏曲プレパラション|Kansō-Kyoku Pureparashon|English version: "Intermezzo: Preparation"}}). Depending on the situation, Brook is also able to produce organic matter such as tears, fecal matter, and even blood from his nose despite not having any organs nor bodily liquids to produce such matter.{{Qref|chap=442|ep=337|Brook answers Luffy's question if he can poop.}}{{Qref|chap=486|ep=378|Brook cries with tears of joy upon hearing Laboon's welfare.}}{{Qref|chap=489|ep=381|Brook gets a nosebleed upon hearing that Mermaids do not wear panties.}}

Brook is able to move and stand up without the presence of tissue and muscles to support him, as well as be capable of getting tired or worn down despite not having any of those factors to begin with. Due to the fruit's powers holding up and moving his light skeletal frame, Brook is given an extremely light body. He can perform seemingly superhuman feats such as jumping extremely high and running on water.{{Qref|chap=443|ep=339|Brook is shown able to jump high and run on water due his light body.}} These allow him to travel great distances and aid him in battle. However, while his light body lets him be lighter than an average person, Brook is not immune from sinking. Brook will still sink like any other Devil Fruit user when placed in water. In fact, while Brook can run on water, he cannot stay above it too long.{{Qref|chap=494|page=2|ep=388}} However, in the anime, it was implied that he could carry at least another person with him while quickly traversing across the surface of a large body of water like this.

Being a skeleton animated by the fruit's powers also allows Brook to do things that most other people cannot do due to their need of tangible living tissue. Not only is he able to use his light weight to execute fast attacks, but his lack of flesh also allows him to execute attacks that would otherwise be harmful, such as shocking himself with electricity and becoming an electrically charged projectile.{{Qref|name=c476}} Having no flesh and organs gives Brook a great advantage against carnivores, even though it will still make him angry, such as a dragon at Punk Hazard, the dragon was chasing Brook, but since he was only bones, the dragon ignored him, and Brook got really mad. On the contrary, canine minks who love to gnaw on bones tend to chase after him due to his physiology. Due to the lack of organs, Brook is able to withstand some deadly attacks to a certain degree. For instance, he was able to withstand his skull being shattered and several of his ribs broken.{{Qref|chap=458|ep=352|Brook survives several attacks from Ryuma that shatter his skull.}}{{Qref|chap=459|chap2=462|ep=352|Brook survives several attacks from Ryuma that shatter his ribs.}} Also, due to the Devil Fruit powers allowing it, Brook has the ability to store objects in his skull by opening it along its crack.

While Brook is able to do these things because of his Devil Fruit supported form, he however can still feel pain, as well as fatigue. However, the fact that he lacks the actual organs means that Brook can fore-go most of the necessities required by humans (i.e., eating, breathing, etc.), having stayed up on his old ship for a long time with nothing to sustain himself with. Based on his own statements and comments from others, despite the lack of any muscles, it appears that he is able to grow stronger through normal training. Though Brook is able to repair broken bones, he believes that all growth functions have stopped. For this reason, Brook puts a lot of effort into protecting his afro, since he would be unable to grow it again if it were cut.{{Qref|name=c487}} However, Brook's belief was incorrect, as he grew 11&nbsp;cm during the two years he was separated from the crew.

After developing the ability to remove his soul from his body, Brook uses the intangibility to his advantage to peek at women, as well as escape imprisonment of any kind while contacting other people for assistance and scouting out things.{{Qref|name=c629}}

[[File:Soul Solid Freezing Sword.png|thumb|left|210px|By mastering his Devil Fruit, Brook is now able to generate a freezing aura.]]

After two years of training, Brook has mastered the use of this Devil Fruit to the extent of knowing its true nature. He reveals that in order for his soul to remain here in this world, it produces a unique and powerful energy that is almost physical in form. He has also mastered the energy his soul emits to the extent that he can reattach his bones by using this energy. Brook can engulf objects such as [[Soul Solid|his sword]] with this energy and thereby summon the Chill of the Underworld.{{Qref|name=c643}}{{Qref|chap=646|page=6-7|ep=566}}{{-}}

===Post-Timeskip Techniques===
[[File:Kasuriuta Fubuki Giri.png|thumb|210px|Kasuriuta: Fubuki Giri.]]

*{{Nihongo|'''Kasuriuta: Fubuki Giri'''|掠り唄 吹雪斬り|Kasuriuta Fubuki Giri|literally meaning "Pastoral Song: Blizzard Slash"}}: Combining his incredible speed and his Devil Fruit ability, Brook does the same thing Yahazu Giri does, but he sheaths his sword from top to bottom and the streak mark he creates with his "chilled" sword freezes the opponent's blood. Brook claims that the wind produced from his sword's slashing in this technique contains the essence of the chilling winds of the underworld itself. This was first used to defeat [[Zeo]].{{Qref|chap=646|page=6-7|ep=566}} In the VIZ manga and Funimation adaptations, this is called '''Song of Scratches - Blizzard Slice'''.{{-}}

[[File:Ekakiuta Hitoyogiri.png|210px|thumb|right|Ekakiuta: Hitoyogiri.]]

*{{Nihongo|'''Ekakiuta: Hitoyogiri'''|絵描き唄 一節斬り|Ekakiuta Hitoyogiri|literally meaning "Drawing Song: One-Joint Slash"}}: Another swift draw-and-sheathing technique, it slices the opponent's torso with three horizontal freezing cuts. It was used to defeat [[Giolla]].{{Qref|chap=722|page=17|ep=653}} In the anime, the freezing effect is missing. In the VIZ manga and Funimation adaptations, this is called '''Painting Song Bamboo Flute Slice'''. ''Ekaki Uta'' is known to be a song for children in Japan that teaches them how to draw an animal or any other figure, while ''hitoyogiri'' is a musical instrument with five fingerholes made from a piece of bamboo with one node.{{Qref|Lee, Riley (1992). ''Yearning for the bell: a study of transmission in the shakuhachi honkyoku tradition.'' [http://www.rileylee.net/Thesis14Mar06%20Folder/chap3.html#3.3.1 Ch 3 Historical Background of Shakuhachi and Honkyoku.]}}{{-}}

[[File:Soul Parade.png|thumb|210px|Soul Parade.]]

*{{Nihongo|'''Soul Parade'''|{{Ruby|魂の|ソウル}} パラード|Souru Parādo}}: A defensive maneuver, Brook holds Soul Solid backhand and blocks an attack, freezing anything, it touches. It was first used to defend against [[Sheepshead]].{{Qref|chap=795|page=7|ep=739}}
**{{Nihongo|'''Eisbahn'''|アイスバーン|Aisubān}}: Brook uses a swift draw-and-sheathing technique to freeze the ground within a certain radius. It was first used to make Sheepshead's steed slip and fall.{{Qref|chap=810|page=14|ep=760}} ''Eisbahn'' is German for "ice rink." In the VIZ manga and Funimation adaptations, this is called '''Ice Burn'''.
**'''Ice Wall''':{{Qref|ep=1044|Ice Wall is named.}} Brook uses a draw-and-sheathing technique to create a large ice wall behind him, erupting from the ground. It was first used to hide [[Black Maria]] and [[Nico Robin]] from view.{{Qref|chap=1021|ep=1044}} In the Funimation adaptations, this is called '''Ice Wall''' though it goes unnamed in the manga.

*{{Nihongo|'''Swallow Banderole'''|{{Ruby|飛燕|スワロー}} バンドゥロル|Suwarō Banduroru}}: Brook jumps towards the opponent and performs a very swift vertical downward slash that cuts and freezes them. The freezing effect is such that it even affects the ground. It was first used to finish one of the last two remaining guards of the Room of Treasure in [[Whole Cake Chateau]].{{Qref|chap=849|page=12|ep=815}}

*{{Nihongo|'''Hanauta Sancho: Tyamasi no Yahazu Giri'''|鼻唄三丁 {{Ruby|魂|テャマスィー}} の矢筈斬り|Hanauta Sanchō: Tyamasī no Yahazu Giri|literally meaning "Three-Verse Humming: Soul Arrow-Notch Slash"}}: Combining ''Hanauta Sancho: Yahazu Giri'' with his Devil Fruit power, Brook jumps into the air and uses a draw-and-sheathing technique to vertically slash his opponent. His speed and light weight allow him to jump high into the air and cut faraway opponents. It was first used against [[Zeus]], and was strong enough to bisect the [[Homies|cloud homie]]. As the technique is imbued with soul power thanks to his Devil Fruit, it even inflicts pain on the homie, which are immune even to the effects of [[Haki]], and could normally only be harmed by an opposing attribute.{{Qref|chap=890|page=16-17|ep=864}} This is called '''Three-Pace Hum Soul Notch Slash''' in the VIZ manga and Funimation subs, while it is called '''Three-Verse Humming Soul Notch Slash''' in the Funimation dub.

*{{Nihongo|'''Cold Soul'''|コールド{{Ruby|魂|ソウル}}|Kōrudo Souru}}: Brook flies out of his skeleton body in soul form and then passes through his target, freezing it with his soul's coldness. It was first used against [[Wanyudo]] to stop him from generating flames for [[Black Maria]]'s polearm.{{Qref|chap=1020|page=12|ep=1043}}

[[File:Phrase d'armes Orchestra.png|thumb|210px|Phrase d'armes: Orchestra.]]

*{{Nihongo|'''Phrase d'armes: Orchestra'''|フラーズ ダルム {{Ruby|管弦楽|オーケストラ}}|Furāzu Darumu: Ōkesutora}}: Brook creates a slash in the shape of a G-clef, which freezes the point of impact on his opponents. It was first used to defeat [[Kunyun]], [[Sarahebi]], [[Nure-Onna]], and [[Tenjo-Sagari]].{{Qref|chap=1021|page=14-15|ep=1044}} ''Phrase d'armes'' is a fencing term which describes the sequence of actions during an assault.

==History==
The fruit was eaten by [[Brook]] about 52 years ago. Thanks to the fruit's powers, his soul was able to return after his death, but he lost his body because of the fog. After one year, he found it, but it was just a pile of bones. But the afro remained intact because it had "strong roots".{{Qref|chap=488|ep=380}}{{Qref|chap=487|ep=380}}

==Anime and Manga Differences==
Brook's soul was originally yellow in the anime, instead of being white and light green as in the manga.{{Qref|vol=64|Brook's soul is shown green on the cover page.}} The anime colors were later updated to match the manga.{{Qref|ep=549|Brook's soul is now green.}}

Also in the anime, when separating his soul from his body, he performs an eerie, ritualistic chant. First, he shouts "Dorororororo!" and then chants {{Nihongo|"bone"|骨/ほね|Hone}} over and over and ends it by shouting {{Nihongo|"Bang! Boom"|ドン! ボーント!|Don! Bōnto!}}.

==Trivia==
*Brook's soul, upon returning to the mortal realm to search for his body, resembles a {{W|hitodama}}, a representation of the recently deceased commonly found in Japanese folklore and pop culture.
*Aside from the standard applications of [[Devil Fruit|awakening]], this is the only known Devil Fruit that requires a specific condition to fully "activate"; in this case, the user must die to trigger the effect.
**In addition, this is the only Devil Fruit to not return to circulation immediately after the user's death. Furthermore, since it has the potential to prevent death by old age during the user's second life, this Devil Fruit could theoretically never return to circulation if its user is never killed.
*Among the [[Straw Hat Pirates]], Brook is the Devil Fruit user with the least amount of named attacks that directly uses his Devil Fruit's abilities. However, Brook does have several named [[Soul Solid|swordsmanship]] techniques that involve the usage of the fruit's abilities.
*In ''[[One Piece Odyssey]]'', one of the [[bounties]] in the [[Memoria]] of [[Dressrosa]] was the self-proclaimed user of this fruit, nicknamed '''[[Biezom|Deathless Biezom]]'''. As the current user, Brook himself notes there cannot be two users with the same devil fruit.
*This fruit is one of the few known to give the user an immunity to drowning, making the standard weakness a non-factor. 
*Before this fruit—and [[zombie]]s—were introduced in the [[Thriller Bark Arc]], the [[One Piece (Anime)|anime]] explored the idea of re-animated corpses at least twice: [[Joke]] in the [[Episode Special 1|first TV special]], and the [[Red Arrow Pirates]] in the [[Baron Omatsuri and the Secret Island|sixth movie]].

