*{{Nihongo|'''Heavenly Feuer Blitz'''|{{Ruby|天上の|ヘヴンリー}} {{Ruby|火雷|フォイアブリッツ}}|Hevunrī Foia Burittsu|literally meaning "The Heavens' Fire Lightning"}}: Big Mom summons both Prometheus and Zeus to unleash a gigantic blast of fire and lightning towards the opponent. This was first seen used 38 years ago against [[Monkey D. Garp]], though Garp managed to withstand the attack.{{Qref|chap=1161|page=11|ep=}}

====Nami====
{{See|Art of Weather/Sorcery Clima-Tact/Zeus}}
*{{Nihongo|'''Zeus Breeze Tempo'''|ゼウスブリーズテンポ|Zeusu Burīzu Tenpo}}: An unwitting attack forced by [[Nami]]. Nami feeds Zeus several '''Black Balls''' and a '''Weather Egg''' with a thundercloud inside, causing him to grow to a massive size, before maneuvering her '''[[Art of Weather/Sorcery Clima-Tact/Grow Up|Clima-Tact]]''' to manipulate them from within Zeus (even against his will) to strike her target with a large lightning attack comprised of both her own and Zeus's full abilities. The force of the thunderbolt was enough to cause [[Charlotte Perospero]] to believe that Big Mom had annihilated the Straw Hats with it.{{Qref|name=c875|chap=875|page=5-7, 10-14|ep=846|Nami uses Zeus to attack Big Mom.}}
[[File:Ninpo Raitei.png|thumb|210px|Ninpo: Raitei.]]
*{{Nihongo|'''Raitei'''|雷霆|Raitei|Meaning "Thunderbolt"}}: After summoning Zeus and feeding him a Weather Egg, Nami swings her Clima-Tact downward with Zeus following the movement and striking her target and surrounding area with a massive electric discharge. It was first used against [[Kurozumi Orochi]].{{Qref|name=c933|chap=933|page=14-16|ep=928|Nami uses Raitei.}} It was also later used to defeat Ulti, successfully defeating the powerful Tobiroppo in one strike. Due to maintaining his cloud form in the midst of this attack, Zeus is capable of moving around and homing in on his target if it misses the first time.{{Qref|name=c1016}} It is called '''Ninpo: Lightning Blast''' in the VIZ manga and Funimation adaptations.
*{{Nihongo|'''Grow Up'''|{{Ruby|成長|グローアップ}}|Gurōappu|literally meaning "Grow to Adulthood"}}: By incorporating the growth abilities of the [[Pop Green]] into the second model, similar to his own [[Usopp's Arsenal/Kuro Kabuto|Kuro Kabuto]], Usopp designed the new Sorcery Clima-Tact to also change size. Whenever Nami squeezes the handle, she can extend the size of the staff, where the new length is determined by the amount of pressure that is applied.{{Qref|chap=822|page=11-12|ep=776|Nami shows off her new Clima-Tact.}} Nami's first usage of this move as an actual method of offense was against [[Charlotte Brûlée]], as an escape measure after the latter had Nami captured in her arms.{{Qref|chap=835|page=7|ep=796|Nami jabs Brûlée with the Clima Tact, causing her to wince.}} With Zeus's inclusion, the attack becomes even stronger, with him manipulating the size and shape of the Clima-Tact to deal heavier blows.
*{{Nihongo|'''Thunder Shark Tempo'''|{{Ruby|電光|サンダー}}{{Ruby|鮫|シャーク}}テンポ|Sandā Shāku Tenpo}}: Nami summons Zeus with her Clima-Tact pointed downward. Once charged, Zeus reshapes himself into a shark-shaped thundercloud filled with lightning as Nami swings the Clima-Tact forward, launching him towards her target. Upon hitting the target, they are shocked with an extreme electrical discharge. It was first used in an attempt to strike down [[Gunko]] of the [[Knights of God]], though she redirected it into Brook instead.{{Qref|chap=1146|page=6-7|ep=1176}}
*{{Nihongo|'''Pouring Rain Tempo'''|{{Ruby|豪雨|ポワリング・レイン}}゠テンポ|Powaringu Rein Tenpo}}: After Zeus absorbs a large quantity of water, Nami has him release it as a heavy rain. It was first used to combat the fire consuming the [[Walrus School]] and [[Owl Library]].{{Qref|chap=1176|page=5-6|ep=}}

