==Early Concepts==
In one of his early design concepts, Zeus was known as the {{Nihongo|'''North Wind'''|北風|Kitakaze}}, rather than "Thundercloud".{{Qref|name=vivre card}} This could mean that Zeus and Prometheus were at some point intended to reference one of Aesop's fables, {{W|The North Wind and the Sun}}.

==Trivia==
*Zeus' name comes from {{W|Zeus|the thunder god of ancient Greek mythology}}.
*Zeus shares the same voice actor as his fellow special [[homies]] [[Prometheus]] and [[Napoleon]].
*Zeus and Prometheus' rivalry may be based on Aesop's fable ''{{W|The North Wind and the Sun}}''. In later retellings of the story, the two entities are personified by the Greek deities {{W|Boreas (god)|Boreas}} and {{W|Helios}}. 
*Zeus' ability to carry Big Mom and fly is similar to Sun Wukong's cloud from [[w:c:mythus:Xi You Ji|''Journey to the West'']].
*Zeus' birthday, June 26, is known as "Thunder Anniversary".{{Qref|name=birth}}
*Zeus' favorite food is the {{W|Cumulonimbus cloud|thunderclouds}} made by [[Nami]].{{Qref|name=vivre card}}
*When he manifested as a cloud from Nami's Clima-Tact after inhabiting it, Zeus suggested Nami give him a new name. Nami called him {{Nihongo|"'''Wata'''"|わた||English version: "Fluff"}}, which comes from the kanji for {{Nihongo|"cotton"|綿}} in Japanese, but Zeus promptly decided to continue using his old name afterwards.{{Qref|chap=1016|page=10|ep=1038}}
**This word also sounds like the Russian word "Vata" (rus. ''Вата''), meaning ordinary cotton wool, a piece of which Zeus also resembles, while in real life people often compare clouds to cotton wool.

