==Personality==
Tama is quick to make friends, trusting and helping [[Monkey D. Luffy]] moments after he assured her he means her no harm.{{Qref|name=debut}} Being a [[Ninja|kunoichi]] in training, she has a habit of starving herself as a means of training her body, forcing it mentally to let go of her hunger.{{Qref|chap=911|page=14-18|ep=894|Tama suffers from starvation.}} She is also very brave, as she stood up to the [[Beasts Pirates]] when they tried stealing her belongings and even attacked one of them after being freed from captivity. Tama has great faith in the [[Kouzuki Family]], as she used their name as a threat to those who upset her.{{Qref|name=c911b|chap=911|page=12|ep=894|Tama describes her encounter with the Beasts Pirates.}} However, she can also be careless, as shown when she revealed her allegiance to the Kouzuki Family to the Beasts Pirates, drank out of a contaminated river and fell ill in the process,{{Qref|name=debut}} and disregarded her master's warnings not to show her powers in front of others, which caught the attention of [[Holed'em]].{{Qref|name=c915|chap=915|page=7|ep=901}}

Tama speaks with an Edo and a {{W|Tōhoku dialect|Tōhoku}} dialect. She tends to end her sentences in {{Nihongo|''de-yansu''|でやんす}}. ''Yansu'' is an auxiliary verb used in the Kansai Dialect, most specifically in the Shiga Prefecture, meaning "to be." Tama also uses the personal pronoun ''ora'' (おら) for herself, which is associated with ruralism.{{Qref|name=debut}}

==Relationships==
===Family===
[[File:Tama at Parents' Grave.png|thumb|210px|Tama at her parents' grave.]]

Tama's parents died when she was still very young and they seemed to have had a caring relationship as Tama brought incense and flowers to their grave while she reassured them that she would survive on her own.{{Qref|name=c1051p9-10|chap=1051|page=9-10|ep=1078}}

Her parents were members of the [[Kurozumi Family]], but the people around Tama are currently unaware of her lineage. Despite her heritage, she holds no loyalty in regards to their plot for revenge; instead, she aids the [[Ninja-Pirate-Mink-Samurai Alliance]] in bringing down the false [[shogun]], [[Kurozumi Orochi]].{{Qref|name=sbs105}}

===Friends===
====Tenguyama Hitetsu====
As Tama's master, Hitetsu cares for her very much, to the point that he attacked [[Monkey D. Luffy]] when he thought Luffy had stolen one of the only two rice meals she has every year.{{Qref|chap=911|page=15-17|ep=894}} He was also angry at Luffy for revealing [[Portgas D. Ace]]'s death, which made Tama sad.{{Qref|chap=912|page=4-5|ep=894}} However, she has no clue that her master is in fact [[Kouzuki Sukiyaki]].

====Portgas D. Ace====
When [[Portgas D. Ace]] visited [[Wano Country|Wano]], Tama formed a bond with him and had wanted to join his crew, but Ace refused based on her current age. However, he did promise that once the two meet again and she becomes a [[Ninja|kunoichi]], he would bring her on board. When [[Monkey D. Luffy]] informed her of [[Summit War of Marineford|Ace's death]], Tama was deeply upset and refused to believe him.{{Qref|name=c912a|chap=912|page=3-4, 7|ep=894}} When Luffy struck [[Holed'em]] with the [[Gomu Gomu no Mi/Gear 2 Techniques|Gomu Gomu no Red Hawk]], Tama stated that he reminded her of Ace.{{Qref|name=c912b|chap=912|page=11-12|ep=897}}

====Komachiyo====
Tama raised [[Komachiyo]] from a little pup, and he was her only companion after her parents died.{{Qref|name=c1051p9-10}} As such, he is very loyal to and protective of Tama.{{Qref|name=c911b}}

====Hihimaru====
While initially antagonistic, [[Hihimaru]] befriended Tama after she fed it some [[Foods#Dango|dango]] and joined her as the group headed toward Tama's home.{{Qref|name=debut}}

====Monkey D. Luffy====
[[Monkey D. Luffy]] inadvertently rescued Tama when her kidnappers attacked him. Because of this, she has immense gratitude and refers to Luffy with a {{Nihongo|"big brother"|アニキ|aniki}} honorific. She even went as far as to give him the rice she was meant to have, even though it is the most she eats all year.{{Qref|name=debut}} However, Tama became furious when Luffy reported [[Portgas D. Ace]]'s death to her.{{Qref|chap=912|page=3-4|ep=894|Luffy reports Ace's death to Tama.}} After she was abducted by [[Gazelleman]] and brought to [[Holed'em]], Tama hoped for Luffy to save her, showing her faith in him.{{Qref|name=c915}} After Luffy freed her from Holed'em, Luffy promised that he would make her life better before leaving [[Wano Country]]. She was initially unaware that Luffy is Ace's brother, though she did notice similarities between the two.{{Qref|chap=918|page=6, 16|ep=906|ep2=908|Luffy's actions remind Tama of Ace.}} After hearing that [[Kaidou]] attacked her, Luffy regretted not taking her to her home safely himself and attacked Kaidou in a fit of rage.{{Qref|name=c923|chap=923|page=5-6|ep=914}} 

When she heard about Luffy's capture, Tama was more concerned about him than her own injuries.{{Qref|name=c925|chap=925|page=14-15|ep=918}} She cares about Luffy so much that she went with the group heading for [[Udon]] to get him out. She was later happy to be reunited with him after his group's takeover of Udon. However, Luffy scolded her for putting herself in danger by coming to the prison. Tama has grown so attached to Luffy that she is seen mostly by his side. Also, she does not like to see Luffy get hurt, even from people he has associated with when he does something that irritates them. Tama later learned from [[Nami]] that Ace was Luffy's brother and felt regretful for how she acted, knowing that Ace's death was also hard for Luffy.{{Qref|name=c999|chap=999|page=9, 15-16|ep=1013|ep2=1014}} After becoming [[Shinobu]]'s kunoichi apprentice, Tama swears that she will join [[Straw Hat Pirates|Luffy's crew]] when she can properly use [[ninjutsu]], to which he accepts.{{Qref|name=c1056}}

====Straw Hat Pirates====
Due to her bond with [[Monkey D. Luffy]], Tama is shown to have become acquainted with his crew, the [[Straw Hat Pirates]]. She gets along well with [[Tony Tony Chopper]] during her time training with him and traveling to [[Udon]] to rescue Luffy. She also helped [[Nami]] and [[Usopp]] by saving them from [[Ulti]] and [[Page One]]. Nami was deeply offended when Ulti smacked Tama when the latter was trying to protect [[Komachiyo]] from Ulti, and Nami was ultimately successful in bringing down Ulti for attacking a child.

====Kouzuki Momonosuke====
Tama befriended the heir of the [[Kouzuki Family]], [[Kouzuki Momonosuke]], when he was staying in Amigasa Village. She has no problem being casual with him, calling him "Momo."{{Qref|name=c928|chap=928|page=17|ep=922|Tama and Momo discuss Hiyori.}} The two further developed their bond during the raid on the [[Udon]] [[Prisoner Mine]], where Tama convinced Momonosuke to enter the facility with her {{Qref|name=c947|chap=947|page=16|ep=947}} and held him in place when he lost his temper at Luffy.{{Qref|name=c950|chap=950|page=5|ep=950}}

Tama has expressed a wish to see Momonosuke become the [[Shogun]] of [[Wano Country]] {{Qref|name=c1004|chap=1004|ep=1019|Tama's Kibi Dango took many Gifters under her control.}}, which she later got to witness after the fall of the [[Beasts Pirates]].{{Qref|name=c1051|chap=1051|page=5-17|ep=1078}}

====Speed====
[[File:Speed and Tama.png|thumb|left|210px|Tama rides on Speed.]]

After [[Kibi Kibi no Mi|taming]] [[Speed]] {{Qref|name=c918|chap=918|page=4-5|ep=906}}, Tama quickly bonded with the Shinuchi, who had become loyal and protective of the girl.{{Qref|name=c919|chap=919|page=2-3|ep=908}} Tama also took to calling her "Umami" (English version: "Horselina"), like Luffy did.{{Qref|chap=925|page=14|ep=918}} Despite being separated during [[Kaidou]]'s attack,{{Qref|name=c923}} Tama later sought out Speed's help in reaching [[Onigashima]] for the [[Raid on Onigashima|raid]], as well as distributing the dangos to [[Beasts Pirates#Gifters|Gifters]].{{Qref|name=c1004}}

Knowing that her dango's effect would wear off after a month, Tama wished for Speed to stay with her forever as a mother, which shocked and moved Speed.{{Qref|name=c1051p7|chap=1051|page=7|ep=1078}}

===Enemies===
====Beasts Pirates====
As an ally of the [[Kouzuki Family]], Tama defies everything the [[Beasts Pirates]] stand for and was kidnapped as a result. While being tied up in a sack, the Beasts Pirates planned to either sell her in the Red Light District or turn her in until [[Monkey D. Luffy]] interfered.{{Qref|name=c911b}} Also, [[Holed'em]] had an interest in her ability to tame animals and tried to force her to use it until Luffy came to her rescue. [[Kaidou]] almost killed her when he saw [[Speed]]'s betrayal.

Tama utilized her ability to turn many of the Beast Pirates' [[Beasts Pirates#Gifters|Gifters]] into her subordinates—including, but not limited to, [[Speed]], [[Babanuki]], [[Briscola]], [[Daifugo]], [[Gazelleman]], [[Mizerka]] and [[Poker]]—causing a huge discord for the [[Beasts Pirates#Tobiroppo|Tobiroppo]], with the intent on having them help the Kouzuki to overthrow the corrupt regime.{{Qref|name=c1004}}

===Other===
====Charlotte Linlin====
After [[Charlotte Linlin|Big Mom]] lost her memories, Tama developed a friendly relationship with her, although she wanted to take advantage of her strength to break [[Monkey D. Luffy]] out of [[Udon]] prison. After breaking into the prison, Big Mom showed willingness to share oshiruko with Tama.{{Qref|chap=945|page=16|ep=944}} Even after she regained her memories, Big Mom still had a soft spot for Tama. However, after Tama witnessed Big Mom's true nature when she had her newest [[Homies|homie]] [[Hera]] consume [[Zeus]], Tama became afraid of her, enraging Big Mom as a result of Tama leaving her, to which she is now determined to kill her former friend as well.{{Qref|chap=1013|page=12-13|ep=1034}}

==Abilities and Powers==
===Physical Abilities===
Initially, Tama was not very strong due to being an 8-year-old girl. However, after some training with [[Shinobu]], she gained enough physical strength to land a solid blow on [[Holed'em]], a [[Beasts Pirates#Gifters|Gifter]] and an [[officer]] of the [[Beasts Pirates]].

===Tactical Skills===
Tama has been shown to be very shrewd for her age, coming up with the idea of manipulating an amnesic [[Charlotte Linlin|Big Mom]] into invading [[Udon]] to break [[Monkey D. Luffy]] free of imprisonment, which later proved crucial in liberating Udon and all of its prisoners to join the Kouzuki Revolution. Tama also ingeniously thought of using her [[Devil Fruit]] powers to tame all the [[Beasts Pirates#Gifters|Gifters]] of the [[Beasts Pirates]] to provide support to the [[Ninja-Pirate-Mink-Samurai Alliance]]'s [[Raid on Onigashima|final battle]] against the Beasts Pirates by having [[Speed]], [[Gazelleman]] and [[Daifugo]] distribute her dangos to other Gifters to turn them against [[Kaidou]], as well as getting [[Usopp]]'s and [[Nami]]'s assistance in her actions.{{Qref|name=c1004}}

===Devil Fruit===
{{See|Kibi Kibi no Mi}}

[[File:Kibi Kibi no Mi Infobox.png|thumb|210px|Tama makes a dango from her cheek.]]

Tama ate the Kibi Kibi no Mi, a [[Paramecia]]-type [[Devil Fruit]] that allows her to create "[[Foods#Dango|dango]]" from her cheeks. They taste good, but they don't satisfy hunger. Any animal that eats one of these dangos will become utterly tame and subservient to Tama, obeying all of her orders and defending her from harm.{{Qref|name=debut}} The effects wear off after one month, at which point an animal may go back to the way they were before and return to the wild or choose to remain her companion, whichever they prefer.{{Qref|name=c1051p7}}

While the dangos usually do not tame humans, those who have eaten functional [[SMILE]]s are susceptible to being tamed due to being part animal.{{Qref|name=c918}}

===Weapons===
Tama was shown using a club against a member of the [[Beasts Pirates]] and had enough strength to knock him out with it in the manga.{{Qref|chap=911|page=9|ep=893|Tama knocks a member of the Beasts Pirates with a club.}}

In the anime, she used leaves while practicing [[ninjutsu]] with [[Tony Tony Chopper]].{{Qref|ep=926}}

===Miscellaneous Skills===
Tama has some experience with cooking rice,{{Qref|chap=911|page=14|ep=894}} and is also capable of weaving [[Straw Hat#Kasa|kasa]] from bamboo.{{Qref|name=c911a}}

==History==
===Past===
[[File:Tama Meets Hitetsu.png|thumb|left|210px|Tama meets Hitetsu who buys a kasa from her.]]

Several years ago, Tama became an orphan after her parents had passed away and being a distant member of the Kurozumi clan, she was unaware of her lineage and Orochi and the rest of his clansmen were also unaware of her and her parents. Later on, she started selling hats but couldn't earn enough money to afford for food. But at one point, [[Kouzuki Sukiyaki|Tenguyama Hitetsu]] came across Tama and bought a hat from her and assured her that the [[Kouzuki Family]]'s warriors will return. Tama was then taken under the protection of Hitetsu.{{Qref|name=c1051p9-10}}

At some point four years ago, [[Portgas D. Ace]] and his crew visited [[Wano Country]] and Tama formed a bond with him. Tama wanted to go out to sea with Ace, but he told her that she was too young at the time. He promised that he would take her with him if she became a [[Ninja|kunoichi]] by the time he returned and Tama waited for him since.{{Qref|chap=911|page=18-19|ep=894}}{{Qref|name=c912a}}

On her eighth birthday, Tama went to the marketplace to buy some rice. However, she was confronted by some [[Beasts Pirates]] scouts and their baboon [[Hihimaru]]. [[Komachiyo]] came to protect her from Hihimaru, but the scouts took her belongings and she mentioned the Kouzuki Family to threaten them, causing them to capture her.{{Qref|name=c911b}}

===Wano Country Saga===
====Wano Country Arc====
Tama was tied up in a sack and begging to be free. The scouts went to confront [[Monkey D. Luffy]], who had arrived in the country illegally. However, Luffy easily overwhelmed them, allowing Tama to free herself out of the sack and knock out one of the scouts.

[[File:Tama Takes Luffy to Her House.png|thumb|210px|Tama takes Luffy to her master's house.]]

Afterward, Tama formally introduced herself to Luffy and tamed [[Hihimaru]] by giving it some [[Kibi Kibi no Mi|Kibi]] [[Foods#Dango|Dango]]. She offered to make food for Luffy out of gratitude and helped him put the [[Thousand Sunny]] in a safe alcove on the coast. They went to her house, where she made rice confections for him before going to drink from the river to quell her hunger. She came back to find her [[Kouzuki Sukiyaki|master]] angered at Luffy for eating the rice, but she told him what had happened. However, she then fell ill due to drinking the contaminated river water polluted by [[Kaidou]]'s factories.{{Qref|name=debut}}

After [[Kouzuki Sukiyaki|Tenguyama Hitetsu]] had revealed that Tama had been waiting for Ace, Luffy informed them of [[Portgas D. Ace]]'s death. Tama was distraught at the news and passed out.{{Qref|name=c912a}} Luffy then decided to take her to a doctor, and as [[Komachiyo]] gave them a ride through the bamboo forest, Tama accused Luffy of lying and explained about the promise Ace made to her. They later entered a wasteland and Tama explained about the terrible environment created by the [[Beasts Pirates]] before falling unconscious again.{{Qref|name=c912b}}

[[File:Tama Eating Oshiruko.png|thumb|left|210px|Tama eats some real food as she recovers from her illness.]]

Tama remained unconscious as Luffy reunited with [[Roronoa Zoro]] after the latter saved a woman from Kaidou's thugs. After Komachiyo dragged Luffy and Zoro away from a battle with Basil Hawkins and his men, the woman that Zoro saved, [[Tsurujo]], told the two [[Straw Hat Pirates|Straw Hats]] to bring Tama to her tea shop. They later arrived at Okobore Town.{{Qref|chap=913|page=2, 10-17|ep=898|ep2=899}}

Tama felt better after receiving some medicine and she reluctantly ate some [[Foods#Oshiruko|oshiruko]] that Tsuru made for her. She then took a nap until Tsuru was attacked by the [[Beasts Pirates#Gifters|Gifter]] [[Batman]]. During the confusion, Tama was abducted by another Gifter, [[Gazelleman]], and taken to Bakura Town.{{Qref|chap=914|page=2-7, 13, 16|ep=900|ep2=901}} Tama was later taken to [[Holed'em]], who took an interest in her after hearing that she tamed [[Hihimaru]], and planned to force her to use her ability.{{Qref|chap=915|page=4-7|ep=901}}

[[File:Holed'em Manga Infobox.png|thumb|210px|Holed'em holds Tama hostage.]]

Holed'em pulled on Tama's cheek, but was unable to get anything out of her. He continued torturing Tama until [[Urashima]] was sent flying into his house by Luffy. Holed'em then confronted Luffy, putting Tama into his lion's mouth and threatening to crush her.{{Qref|chap=916|page=10-11, 18-19|ep=903|ep2=904}} In a blink of an eye, Luffy attacked the lion head and freed Tama. After finding out that Holed'em had used pliers to pull on Tama's cheek, Luffy dropped Tama in midair and turned around to strike Holed'em with a powerful Red Hawk punch.{{Qref|chap=917|page=6-11, 13-17|ep=905}}

With Holed'em defeated, Luffy then grabbed Tama again and ran away with her on the back of [[Speed]], whom he mistook for a horse. Speed got angry, but quickly became subservient to Luffy and Tama after Tama offered some kibi dango at Luffy's request. They made their way to Okobore Town with the supply of food stolen from the Beasts Pirates. As Tama ate an apple, Luffy promised her that she would not go hungry again.{{Qref|chap=918|page=2-6, 15-16|ep=906|ep2=908}}

Tama then parted ways with Luffy and went back to her home by riding on Speed's back.{{Qref|name=c919}} On the way, both Tama and Speed were attacked by Kaidou when the Emperor discovered them and Tama was left lying bloodied on the ground.{{Qref|name=c923}} She was found by [[Inuarashi]], who took her into the forest to receive treatment.{{Qref|chap=924|page=10|ep=916}} Tama was then returned to her home where she was treated by [[Tony Tony Chopper]] and some of the [[Mink Tribe|minks]]. When Tama was worried about Luffy, Chopper assured her that Luffy has incredible recovery speed, and his will would not be broken. He also added that [[Raizo]] was planning on rescuing him.{{Qref|name=c925}}

While [[Kouzuki Momonosuke]] was practicing swordsmanship in Amigasa Village, Tama asked him about his [[Kouzuki Hiyori|sister]], whom Momonosuke believed to still be alive. Tama commented that it would be nice if Momonosuke could meet her, but he stated that he could not reunite with her until the defeat of both the shogun and Kaidou.{{Qref|name=c928}}

[[File:Big Mom Goes to Udon.png|thumb|left|210px|Tama's group takes Big Mom to Udon.]]

Tama, Chopper, [[Kikunojo]] and Momonosuke then went to Kuri Beach where they encountered an amnesiac Big Mom.{{Qref|chap=931|page=14-17|ep=926}} On the following morning, Tama's group took Big Mom to Okobore Town. Although Chopper was worried about Big Mom regaining her memories, Tama insisted on taking her to [[Udon]], which Chopper reluctantly agreed with.{{Qref|chap=933|page=17|ep=928}} The group then traveled to Udon, with Big Mom having tamed a [[Animal Species/Wano Country Saga#Wanizame|Wanizame]] to carry them there. On the way there, Tama spoke to [[Kouzuki Sukiyaki|Tenguyama Hitetsu]] through a [[Animal Species/Wano Country Saga#Smart Tanishi|Smart Tanishi]]. Hitetsu objected to their quest and urged Tama to return to Amigasa Village, but Tama continued on with her group's journey.{{Qref|chap=934|page=4-7|ep=929}} During the journey, Tama and Big Mom happily talked about oshiruko.{{Qref|chap=937|page=3|ep=933}} After night fell, the group eventually arrived at Udon.{{Qref|chap=940|page=17|ep=937}}

On the next day, Tama's group arrived at the Prisoner Mines after Big Mom had broken through the front gate. Kiku told Tama and Momonosuke to hide before proceeding with Chopper.{{Qref|chap=945|page=14-16|ep=944}} When the emergency gates began to close, Tama and Momonosuke entered the Prisoner Mines.{{Qref|name=c947}}

While hiding, Tama and Momonosuke witnessed Luffy persuading the prisoners to rebel against the Beasts Pirates, prompting Tama to remember Luffy's promise to her.{{Qref|chap=949|page=11-13|ep=949}} After the prison takeover, Tama reunited with Luffy though the latter was in a serious condition from being infected with the [[Mummy (Virus)|Mummy virus]].{{Qref|name=c950}}

Tama tamed [[Babanuki]] and had him give a false report to [[Queen]].{{Qref|chap=952|page=6-7|ep=953}} After Luffy had finished his training in Udon, Tama returned to Amigasa Village with him and Chopper two days before the [[raid on Onigashima]].{{Qref|chap=955|page=10|ep=956}} At some point, Tama tamed [[Daifugo]] and Gazelleman.

Prior to the raid, Tama spoke to Speed and requested her assistance. During the [[Fire Festival]], she went to Onigashima on Speed's ship along with Speed, Daifugo, Gazelleman, Komachiyo and Hihimaru. On the way, Tama created many dangos for her allies to distribute to the Beasts Pirates.{{Qref|name=c1004}} After arriving, Tama, Komachiyo and Hihimaru managed to rescue [[Nami]] and [[Usopp]] from [[Ulti]] and [[Page One]].{{Qref|chap=995|page=17|ep=1008}} Tama and Komachiyo fled with the two Straw Hats while Hihimaru stayed behind to stall the two Tobiroppo.{{Qref|chap=996|ep=1009}} As they were talking about Ace while riding on Komachiyo, Nami revealed to Tama that Ace was Luffy's brother.{{Qref|name=c999}}

[[File:Tama Commanding Gifters.png|thumb|210px|Tama participates in the raid by commanding allied Gifters.]]

Tama and her group used her dangos to turn several Gifters into allies. As they were pursued by Ulti and Page One, they went through the area where [[Franky]] and [[Sasaki]] were fighting and they converted Sasaki's subordinates as well.{{Qref|name=c1004}} As Tama made her way to the Live Stage, Page One jumped onto Komachiyo's back, but Usopp's projectiles forced Page One to let go. They then ran across an angry Big Mom, much to their horror. Tama called out to her and she switched into "Mother Mode" and happily talked with the little girl, who was delighted to learn that Big Mom had regained her memory. Tama reluctantly informed her about the Beast Pirates destroying Okobore Town, which refueled Big Mom's anger. Tama continued on toward the stage while Big Mom attacked Page One {{Qref|chap=1011|page=11-19|ep=1028|ep2=1031}}, knocking him unconscious. While Ulti confronted Big Mom, Tama and the others fled on Komachiyo, but Ulti charged head first into the [[Animal Species/Wano Country Saga#Komainu|komainu]]. Tama cried as Ulti began torturing Komachiyo, so Ulti struck her, telling her to be quiet. This angered Big Mom and Nami, who electrocuted Ulti in retaliation.{{Qref|chap=1012|page=11-15|ep=1032}} After Big Mom helped take down the [[Beasts Pirates#Tobiroppo|Tobiroppo]], Usopp and Nami carried the injured Tama toward the Live Stage. However, Big Mom plucked Tama out of Usopp's arms, placed her to the side and prepares to attack the Straw Hats. Tama pleaded that they were her friends, but Big Mom ignored her. While Big Mom and Nami were distracted by [[Zeus]]' return, Usopp picked Tama back up. Seeing Tama run from her as well, Big Mom was furious and attacked her and the Straw Hats, but [[Eustass Kid]] stopped the Emperor.{{Qref|chap=1013|page=2-15|ep=1033|ep2=1034}}

As they ran, Tama cried at hearing the announcement that [[Kaidou]] had defeated Luffy {{Qref|chap=1014|page=8-9|ep=1035}} and then cried again when Momonosuke announced that Luffy was still alive.{{Qref|chap=1015|page=12-16|ep=1036|ep2=1037}} As they reached the Live Stage, Ulti caught up to them, knocking down Usopp and grabbing Tama. Usopp used Sargasso to free Tama from Ulti's grasp while Nami and Zeus electrocuted Ulti again. [[Bao Huang]], who had been interrupted during a broadcast, accidentally announced Ulti's defeat to the whole castle, so Usopp captured the Shinuchi and had Tama use her as a loudspeaker.{{Qref|chap=1016|page=5-13|ep=1037|ep2=1038}} When [[Queen]] turned to look at Tama, she briefly fainted but, with Usopp and Nami's encouragement, stood back up and ordered the Gifters to fight for Luffy and Momonosuke and beat Kaidou. The Gifters who had been fed Tama's kibi dangos then turned against the fellow Beasts Pirates. After realizing what Tama had done, Queen prepared to fire his laser at her, but [[Sanji]] kicked him and interrupted the attack while Usopp and Nami fled with Tama.{{Qref|chap=1017|page=2, 5-10|ep=1038|ep2=1039}}

As Tama and the Straw Hats fled, Daifugo fought off the Beasts Pirates chasing them and Speed carried them. Gazelleman also informed Tama that the Gifters would look after Komachiyo, which delighted her.{{Qref|chap=1018|page=2-4|ep=1039}} After reuniting with Komachiyo, Tama and the others stumbled across [[Kin'emon]]'s lower body. While Usopp and [[Hamlet]] split off to rescue the samurai,{{Qref|chap=1030|page=4-6|ep=1055}} the rest sought shelter in the Beasts' Bath where [[Polo Marco|Marco]] checked over Komachiyo and Hihimaru.{{Qref|chap=1041|page=12|ep=1068}} When Kaidou descended from the roof and announced Luffy's death, Tama cried while Nami accused Kaidou of lying. Marco then defended Nami from Kaidou's retaliatory fire breath and Tama ran to Nami's side.{{Qref|chap=1043|page=8-10|ep=1070}} When she and Nami learned that Luffy was still alive, both of them were in tears.{{Qref|chap=1044|page=3|ep=1071}} Tama was encouraged by Nami to believed in Luffy, and later fainted when she witnessed Luffy's giant head slammed into the rooftop.{{Qref|ep=1072|chap=1045|page=12-13}}

After [[Nekomamushi]] had announced Kaidou's defeat, Tama and the rest of the alliance celebrated.{{Qref|chap=1050|page=8}} Later, Usopp asked Tama how long her powers last and she reveals that the gifters will turn back to normal after a month, but some also stayed tame. Speed then told Tama that she wants to stay with her as her master and Tama happily responds to Speed that she wants her to stay with her like a mother forever, to which Speed became touched by what Tama had told her. As Momonosuke announced the citizens freedom, Tama became shocked and thought back to when her parents died working in the factories and when she first met Hitetsu. She then jumped into Nami's arms and started crying. Later, a tearing Tama watched Momonosuke's speech.{{Qref|name=c1051}}

After the festival, Tama began to work as [[Shinobu]]'s apprentice and she vowed to join Luffy's crew when she became a better kunoichi.{{Qref|name=c1056}}

===Final Saga===
====Egghead Arc====
Tama ate dango while listening, alongside Shinobu, Momonosuke, and Kin'emon, to [[Vegapunk]]'s worldwide broadcast.{{Qref|chap=1115|page=2|ep=1148}}{{Qref|chap=1116|page=8|ep=1149}}

====Oni Child Yamato's Golden Harvest Surrogate Pilgrimage====
[[File:Tama Kicks Holed'em.png|thumb|left|220px|Tama frees herself and kicks Holed'em.]]

Tama was practicing kunai-throwing when [[Yamato]] came to visit. Afterwards, Tama and Yamato took a nap, during which Yasuie's sword was stolen.{{Qref|cover=1129|cover2=1130}} After being joined by Speed and Komachiyo they began pursuing the thief.{{Qref|cover=1131}} They all arrived in [[Udon]] during the reconstruction of the region's castle. Suddenly Holed'em ambushed them, knocking Speed aside and taking Tama hostage, and demanded the group's valuables. However, thanks to her kunoichi training, Tama was able to break free of Holed'em's grip and deliver a devastating kick. The group then bound Holed'em and forced him to take them to his base.{{Qref|cover=1132|cover2=1136}} Tama and Yamato infiltrated the base{{Qref|cover=1137}} and found that [[Who's-Who]] had taken the sword, along with many kidnapped women.{{Qref|cover=1138}} After Yamato took down Who's-Who, she helped free the women and [[Minatomo (Wano)|Minatomo]], who was also kidnapped.{{Qref|cover=1142|cover2=1144}} Afterwards, Yamato left Tama and Speed with Raizo and he left Udon with [[Ulti]] and [[Page One]], who accompanied him as his followers.{{Qref|name=c1146|cover=1146}}

==Anime and Manga Differences==
[[File:Tama and Luffy Episode 1084.png|thumb|210px|Tama and Luffy's anime-original farewell.]]

Tama is featured in a segment of the [[Canon#Fillers|anime-original]] farewell episode before the [[Straw Hat Pirates]] depart from [[Wano Country]]. The segment includes a final interaction between Tama and [[Monkey D. Luffy|Luffy]] that takes place after the scene in the castle where she introduced herself as [[Shinobu]]'s new apprentice. Luffy and Tama visit the [[Kuri#Okobore Town|Okobore Town]] rebuilding site at sunset and enjoy oshiruko made by [[Tsurujo]]. Tama is sad that Luffy is leaving, but he cheers her up, and Tama declares her intention to become stronger once more.{{Qref|ep=1084|Tama and Luffy's anime-only story.}}

