'''S-Hawk''' is one of the [[Seraphim]] and a [[Lunarian]]-based [[Cloning|clone]] of [[Dracule Mihawk]].{{Qref|name=debut}}{{Qref|name=c1068|chap=1068|page=11|ep=1099|S-Hawk is mobilized on Egghead.}}

Due to his actions and role, he is a supporting antagonist in the [[Egghead Arc]].

==Appearance==
S-Hawk resembles Mihawk as a child, but is significantly larger in size. He also possesses [[Lunarians|lunarian]] traits, such as brown skin, black wings, and white hair.{{Qref|name=debut}} His irises have additional rings similar to Mihawk's, but his pupils are star-shaped like the other Seraphim. A section of his right forearm is replaced by a tube that is filled with [[Green Blood]].{{Qref|name=c1069|chap=1069|ep=1100}}

===Gallery===
{{Gallery|height=150|width=150|position=center|captionalign=center
|S-Hawk Pupils.png|S-Hawk's pupils.
|S-Hawk Anime Concept Art.png|S-Hawk's anime concept art.
}}

==Personality==
S-Hawk has not displayed any personality outside of his obedience to the [[Marines]] and [[Vegapunk]] and aggression towards his designated targets.{{Qref|name=debut}} Zoro has regarded S-Hawk as possessing more humanity than the original Dracule Mihawk.{{Qref|name=ch1073}}

==Abilities and Powers==
S-Hawk is one of the Seraphim, which Vegapunk describes as the pinnacle of his scientific achievements and the "Strongest Form of Humanity."{{Qref|chap=1070|page=8|ep=1101}}

===Pacifista Body===
Like other [[Pacifista]], S-Hawk was given the ability to fire [[laser]]s from his palm as a result of Vegapunk's research.{{Qref|name=debut}}

===Fire Manipulation===
As an artificial [[Lunarians|lunarian]], S-Hawk possesses flames on his back that are linked to his tremendous resilience as a lunarian.{{Qref|name=debut}} S-Hawk is sturdy enough to withstand Blackbeard's attack, and also a combined attack from [[Roronoa Zoro]] and [[Kaku]].{{Qref|name=c1076}}

===Swordsmanship===
Like the original Mihawk, S-Hawk is an extremely skilled [[swordsman]]. His attack forced [[Blackbeard]] to use [[Haki/Armament Haki|Armament Haki]] for defense and sliced off a large portion of [[Amazon Lily]]'s central mountain.{{Qref|name=debut}} He was also able to hold his own against [[Roronoa Zoro]], a tremendously powerful master swordsman.

===Devil Fruit===
{{Main|Supa Supa no Mi}}
[[File:Artificial Supa Supa no Mi.png|thumb|210px|S-Hawk turns his leg into a blade.]]

Via the [[Green Blood]], S-Hawk possesses an artificial version of [[Daz Bonez]]'s Supa Supa no Mi, allowing him to turn any part of his body into sharp steel blades. He has used this ability to transform his leg into blade to augment his kicks and create a ranged slicing attack.{{Qref|name=c1076}} In the Anime, S-Hawk's usage of the Supa Supa no Mi mirrors that of Daz Bonez, as like him he attacks with a variety of hand to hand techniques that are enhanced by the effects of his Devil Fruit. Similarly to Daz Bonez, he also has the ability to sprout blades on his feet, allowing him to skate on solid ground as if it were ice.{{Qref|ep=1109}}

===Haki===
{{Main|Haki}}

S-Hawk is able to use [[Haki/Observation Haki|Observation]] and [[Haki/Armament Haki|Armament Haki]].{{Qref|name=vivre card}}

===Weapons===
S-Hawk wields a sword shaped similarly to [[Yoru]], though it is less ornate and its blade is not black.

==History==
===Wano Country Saga===
====Wano Country Arc====
[[File:S-Hawk Vs Blackbeard Pirates.png|thumb|left|210px|S-Hawk facing the Blackbeard Pirates.]]

S-Hawk was brought to [[Amazon Lily]] together with [[S-Snake]] for the mission of capturing [[Boa Hancock]]. During the battle, he clashed with the invading Blackbeard and ended up cutting off a large portion of the island. After the majority of the [[Marines]] were [[Mero Mero no Mi|petrified]], [[Koby]] ordered S-Hawk to stop firing lasers to prevent damage to the statues. S-Hawk received no visible injuries during the mission, but was eventually withdrawn by order of the Marines.{{Qref|name=debut}} Some time later, S-Hawk returned to [[Egghead]].{{Qref|name=c1068}}{{-}}

===Final Saga===
====Egghead Arc====
[[File:S-Hawk Vs Government Officials.png|thumb|210px|S-Hawk defending Egghead.]]

Weeks later, upon [[CP0]] infiltrating Egghead in order to kill Vegapunk and his satellites, [[Shaka]] had S-Hawk, S-Snake, and [[S-Shark]] deployed under the command of [[Sentomaru]].{{Qref|name=c1068}} While [[Monkey D. Luffy]] and [[Rob Lucci]] began fighting, the three Seraphim met up with Sentomaru. The group encountered the invading government agents, during which Sentomaru instructed both S-Hawk and S-Shark to hold back CP0 while S-Snake assisted the [[Straw Hat Pirates]] with fleeing with Vegapunk.{{Qref|name=c1069}} Obeying Sentomaru's commands, the three Seraphim were joined by [[S-Bear]] with assaulting the government agents until Sentomaru succumbed to his injuries, resulting in the four Seraphim following CP0's command.{{Qref|chap=1070|page=5, 16-17|ep=1101|ep2=1102}}

[[File:Zoro vs. S-Hawk.png|thumb|left|210px|S-Hawk's attempted ambush on Lilith is stopped by Zoro.]]

Upon CP0 infiltrating Egghead's Labophase while its defense system was deactivated, the four Serapim took the initative to follow the assassins. When they arrived, Lucci ordered them to destroy Vegapunk's laboratory before he comes out, leading to them damaging the building's structure using a range of attacks.{{Qref|chap=1072|page=12-13, 15-16|ep=1104}} When [[Lilith]] came out of the lab to command them to cease their attacks, S-Hawk was aiming at her, ready to strike at her, only to be interrupted and engaged in a sword clash with [[Roronoa Zoro]], who remarked his similarities towards Mihawk. When [[Edison]] commanded all the Seraphim to stand down, S-Hawk followed the order.{{Qref|name=ch1073|chap=1073|page=5-9|ep=1105}}

[[File:Zoro & Kaku Team.png|thumb|right|210px|S-Hawk is attacked by Zoro and Kaku.]]

While Vegapunk's Satellites and [[Straw Hat Pirates]] searched for the missing Stella within the Labophase, S-Hawk and S-Bear began targeting Kaku and Lucci while they were restrained and unconscious, prompting Zoro to get assistance from Luffy to confront them. Joined by [[Shaka]], the two Seraphim were unaffected by his order to stop, and continued their attacks.{{Qref|chap=1075|page=13-15|ep=1108}} The pressure of the CP0 being targeted leads to them being freed by the Straw Hats to fight the Seraphim, resulting in Zoro and [[Kaku]] engaging S-Hawk in combat,{{Qref|name=c1076|chap=1076|page=3-6, 8-9|ep=1108|ep2=1109}} but they are unable to do any lasting damage to S-Hawk.{{Qref|chap=1077|page=6|ep=1110}} S-Hawk then left to go for the weaker targets.{{Qref|chap=1078|page=8|ep=1111}} 

At some point, he and the other Seraphim were captured in [[seastone]] bubbles and left in the laboratory's basement with the imprisoned [[Cipher Pol]] agents.{{Qref|chap=1090|page=6-7|ep=1124|The Seraphim are captured.}}

After [[Ethanbaron V. Nusjuro|Nusjuro]] cut the Labophase, S-Hawk, the other Seraphim, and the imprisoned Cipher Pol agents all fell to the Fabiriophase.{{Qref|chap=1115|page=10-11|ep=1149|Nusjuro cuts the Labophase.}} They were then inhaled by [[Shepherd Ju Peter]]{{Qref|chap=1116|page=11|ep=1149}} and spat out indiscriminately over the ships of the Marines and the Giant Warrior Pirates.{{Qref|chap=1119|page=10|ep=1151}} Following the Egghead Incident, the Seraphim were recharged and shipped out from Egghead by the Marines.{{Qref|chap=1125|page=2|ep=1155}}

