The '''Pirate Bear''', nicknamed {{Nihongo|'''Paw-san'''|ポーさん|Pō-san}}, is a bear who can be recruited by the [[Straw Hat Pirates]] in ''[[Grand Line Dream Adventure Log]]''.{{Qref|name=debut}}

==Appearance==
The Pirate Bear is large bear with purple fur and red eyes. It has a white skull and crossbones painted on its body.

==Personality==
The Pirate Bear admires [[pirate]]s and wanted to become one after hearing about [[Monkey D. Luffy|Luffy]].{{Qref|name=debut}}

==Abilities and Powers==
The Pirate Bear can take part in a combination attack called {{Nihongo|'''Animal Rush'''|アニマルラッシュ|Animaru Rasshu}} with the [[Pirate Penguin]]. This technique is triggered by either [[Tony Tony Chopper|Chopper]] or [[Chouchou]], and features the Pirate Bear throwing the Pirate Penguin at an enemy with its beak aimed at them.{{Qref|name=debut}}

==History==
===Grand Line Dream Adventure Log===
The Pirate Bear met [[Apis]] on [[Warship Island]] and the two [[Hiso Hiso no Mi|conversed]]. Apis told the bear about [[Monkey D. Luffy|Luffy]], which made it want to join the [[Straw Hat Pirates]].

When the [[Straw Hat Pirates]] visited [[Bokuden]]'s house, they found Apis and the Pirate Bear in the kitchen. Apis asked the crew to take the bear with them, and the bear politely requested the same. Luffy agreed, and the bear joined the crew.{{Qref|name=debut}}

==Trivia==
*The Pirate Bear is modeled after a bear featured on the [[Cover Page#Color Covers|color cover]] of [[Chapter 7]], although the coloration of its fur and eyes differs.{{Qref|name=c7}} The description of the Pirate Bear mentions the events of the cover, indicating that they are indeed one and the same.{{Qref|name=debut}}
**Artwork of the Pirate Bear, based on its initial depiction on Chapter 7's cover, would later reappear on the cover of ''[[Weekly Shonen Jump]]'''s 1998 issue 26.

